## 14. Quick revision sheet

## Remember these before an interview

Checked exception

Must be caught or declared when required by the compiler.

Unchecked exception

A `RuntimeException` subclass; catching or declaring it is not mandatory.

`throw`

Throws an exception object.

`throws`

Declares exception types in a method signature.

`finally`

Normally executes during cleanup when leaving a `try`/`catch` construct.

Try-with-resources

Automatically closes supported resources.
